==== Buttons ====
-> [[docs:guide-user:hardware:hardware.button]] on howto use and configure the hardware button(s).

The MikroTik RB450Gx4 has the following buttons:

^ BUTTON   ^ Event   ^
| Reset    | reset   |
| Reset jumper hole   | not used |

The reset jumper hole is located in the corner, next to the flash chip. It is activated by closing the two sides of the hole with a metallic object (e.g. a screwdriver) and used to reset RouterBOOT to factory settings. Currently not used in OpenWrt.
{{:media:mikrotik:rb450gx4_top_reset_hole.jpg?direct&400|}}

